Qwen3-ASR: a GGUF may name its own languages for the prompt prefix

Bokfink (NB-ASR Bokfink02, a Qwen3-ASR fine-tune) needs the prefixes `language Norwegian<asr_text>` and
`language Norwegian Nynorsk<asr_text>`, which the fixed table of Qwen's 30 languages cannot give. The loader
reads an optional stt.qwen3_asr.language_names array, one name per general.languages entry, and the prefix
lookup tries it before the fixed table. Without the key nothing changes. This is the library half of
research/bokfink/transcribe-cpp-qwen3-asr-language-names.patch; the converter half writes the key. Evidence:
docs/research/bokfink-gguf.md, «Language prefixes».

Against transcribe.cpp 4a4e08f99c62ae1036551c259477fe4f3127f092 (v0.5.1), paths as in the
transcribe-cpp-sys crate. Skald carries it until upstream releases this change or one like it.

